so allow me to quickly
implement it and we can move forward.

112
00:06:18.633 --> 00:06:19.266
Similar to

113
00:06:19.266 --> 00:06:22.466
earlier, what you will do
is to provide the prompt

114
00:06:22.533 --> 00:06:26.933
that will contain the tool descriptions
and the user query to your LLM.

115
00:06:27.900 --> 00:06:30.233
Let's say that you want the LLM to draw

116
00:06:30.233 --> 00:06:33.233
a pink clown face with the red nose.

117
00:06:33.266 --> 00:06:36.266
Format this and create the prompt.

118
00:06:38.300 --> 00:06:41.300
Finally, take a look at the prompt
you have.

119
00:06:41.733 --> 00:06:44.666
As you can see,
you have the function description

120
00:06:44.666 --> 00:06:47.666
identified with the function tag.

121
00:06:47.666 --> 00:06:50.200
You can see that the LLM can identify

122
00:06:50.200 --> 00:06:53.333
from the function description
and the user query.

123
00:06:53.433 --> 00:06:57.633
First that it should invoke this function,
and second,

124
00:06:57.933 --> 00:07:02.300
it can fill in the arguments
face color, eye color, and nose color.

125
00:07:02.300 --> 00:07:05.333
From the information in the user query.

126
00:07:06.366 --> 00:07:09.233
Here and here.

127
00:07:09.233 --> 00:07:12.066
Now call the function-calling LLM.

128
00:07:12.066 --> 00:07:15.066
And use it to look at the code string
that it has generated.

129
00:07:15.533 --> 00:07:18.700
It has extracted the necessary information

130
00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:22.333
from the user prompt,
which is the face color being pink.

131
00:07:22.466 --> 00:07:24.100
And the nose color being red.

132
00:07:25.366 --> 00:07:27.733
Now you will run it.

133
00:07:27.733 --> 00:07:29.600
In this case, it's a pink clown face

134
00:07:29.600 --> 00:07:32.600
with the red nose,
which is exactly what we expected.

135
00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:36.166
Now let's try writing your own clown.

136
00:07:36.166 --> 00:07:40.166
Here is a framework
where you can enter your own query

137
00:07:40.466 --> 00:07:43.466
or change the prompt
and create your own clown.

138
00:07:43.466 --> 00:07:44.966
Give it a try.

139
00:07:44.966 --> 00:07:49.966
So Raven is not the only LLM
that's capable of issuing function calls.

140
00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:54.933
Let's try using OpenAI's function-calling
on the same example.

141
00:07:55.500 --> 00:07:59.666
You'll import the necessary attributes,
and try to use the GPT-3.5

142
00:07:59.766 --> 00:08:01.633
turbo model.

143
00:08:01.633 --> 00:08:05.666
For this example,
you build a client and you.

144
00:08:05.666 --> 00:08:09.533
you'll also build a helper function
